[C1] PASS the coded left eigenvectors invert the right ones: max |R R^-1 - I| / (max|R| max|R^-1|) over 200 Roe states = 2.8e-18
[C2] PASS R Lambda R^-1 is the flux Jacobian at the Roe state, and A (q_R - q_L) = F_R - F_L for one gamma: max relative errors 7.5e-16 and 6.6e-15 over 200 pairs
[C3] PASS a, b, c are the Jacobian of Q/dt + the Roe-flux divergence with |A| frozen, on a spherical shell: max block error relative to the block size, central differences: 8.2e-09
[C4] PASS the frozen-m_t partial (3 x 3) solve equals the full one restricted to rho, rho u, E when v = w = 0, and differs when v != 0: relative difference 3.3e-16 at v = 0, 3.7e-03 at v = 50 m/s
[C5] PASS a solid cell has a = I/dt, b = c = 0, and its fluid neighbour sees a mirror whatever the solid holds: solid row exact; neighbour block change when the solid cell's state is replaced: 0.0e+00
[C6] PASS the derivatives of the row residual are the blocks of eq-ch07-vic-blocks, with I/dt_c on the diagonal and the gravity Jacobian Phi subtracted: A_i, B_i, C_i exact on generic 2 x 2 blocks
[C7] PASS under a uniform tangential wind with q_t = 0 the full solve keeps dm_t = v_t drho and the folded partial solve equals it on rho, rho u, E; the frozen-m_t partial solve does not: v = (50, 0) m/s: dm_t - v_t drho 1.5e-14, folded 7.9e-15, frozen 6.7e-02 relative; v = (400, -30) m/s: dm_t - v_t drho 1.9e-15, folded 4.2e-15, frozen 2.1e+00 relative
